### Biliary Atresia

Characterized by obliteration of extrahepatic bile ducts in neonates. Portal areas are expanded with bile duct proliferation, ductular reaction, portal fibrosis and cholestasis.

### Acute Cholecystitis

Thickened, edematous gallbladder wall with prominent neutrophilic infiltration. Mucosal ulceration and necrosis may be seen.

### Chronic Cholecystitis

Thickened, fibrotic wall with chronic lymphoplasmacytic inflammation. Rokitansky-Aschoff sinuses are typical.

### Gallbladder Carcinoma

Often develops in a background of chronic cholecystitis. Glandular or solid tumor areas with significant cytologic atypia and stromal invasion.
